# Review: S3Plugin

The plugin is thin: the connector lives in `src/capabilities/connector.ts`, and the backend, URI
handling and SigV4 signer moved to `@dxos/blob/s3` (`packages/core/echo/blob/src/s3`) with the
database bindings in `@dxos/compute-runtime` (`createS3Host`), so EDGE can register the same
backend. Addressing and signing are solid and tested against AWS's published vectors. The two
divergences: the credential form asks for bucket and endpoint separately and rejects empty fields
in the schema and `onValidate` rather than in `onSubmit`; and an unsigned read treats any 4xx as
a miss (R2 answers 400 for a private bucket), not only 404 and 403. The backend wiring
(`createS3BlobBackend`, `createS3Host`) has no test of its own.

Of 6 items: 3 done, 0 untested, 1 partial, 2 diverged, 0 missing.

