## Verdicts

```mdl
verdict S3Uri: Blobs are addressed s3://<host>/<spaceId>/<contentHash>, and the host is the credential's source.
  status: done
  evidence: [github:dxos/dxos/packages/core/echo/blob/src/s3/s3-uri.ts#S3Uri, github:dxos/dxos/packages/core/echo/blob/src/s3/s3-uri.ts#objectKey, github:dxos/dxos/packages/core/echo/blob/src/s3/s3-uri.ts#parseUri]
  tests: [github:dxos/dxos/packages/core/echo/blob/src/s3/s3-uri.test.ts]
```

```mdl
verdict S3Connector: The credential-form connector exists, but the form splits bucket from endpoint and validates before submit.
  status: diverged
  evidence: [github:dxos/dxos/packages/plugins/plugin-s3/src/capabilities/connector.ts#createS3ConnectorEntry, github:dxos/dxos/packages/plugins/plugin-s3/src/capabilities/connector.ts#composeHost, github:dxos/dxos/packages/plugins/plugin-s3/dx.config.ts]
  tests: [github:dxos/dxos/packages/plugins/plugin-s3/src/capabilities/connector.test.ts, github:dxos/dxos/packages/core/echo/blob/src/s3/s3-client.test.ts]
  walkthrough:
    - The lazy module activates the connector on ConnectorEvents.Start. github:dxos/dxos/packages/plugins/plugin-s3/dx.config.ts
    - The entry joins bucket and endpoint into a bare lowercase host and builds the AccessToken and Connection. github:dxos/dxos/packages/plugins/plugin-s3/src/capabilities/connector.ts#createS3ConnectorEntry
    - testConnection probes a missing key with a signed HEAD and tells 404 from 403. github:dxos/dxos/packages/core/echo/blob/src/s3/s3-client.ts#probeAccess
  note: |
    The form is `{ name?, bucket, endpoint, accessKeyId, secretAccessKey }`, not `{ endpoint, accessKeyId, secretAccessKey }`;
    `composeHost` joins bucket and endpoint. Empty fields are rejected by `Schema.NonEmptyString` and `onValidate`,
    so `onSubmit` never fails. Connector source, label, AccessToken mapping and the HEAD probe match the spec.
    `connector.test.ts` covers only host normalization; the probe is tested in `s3-client.test.ts`.
```

```mdl
verdict S3BlobBackend: The backend registers under s3 on FileEvents.Start and signs put/get/has/getUrl, but unsigned reads treat any 4xx as a miss.
  status: partial
  evidence: [github:dxos/dxos/packages/plugins/plugin-s3/src/capabilities/blob-backend.ts, github:dxos/dxos/packages/core/echo/blob/src/s3/blob-backend.ts#createS3BlobBackend, github:dxos/dxos/packages/core/compute/compute-runtime/src/services/s3-host.ts#createS3Host, github:dxos/dxos/packages/core/echo/blob/src/s3/s3-client.ts#getObjectUrl]
  tests: [github:dxos/dxos/packages/core/echo/blob/src/s3/s3-client.test.ts]
  walkthrough:
    - The plugin module registers the backend on the client graph and contributes FileCapabilities.Backend. github:dxos/dxos/packages/plugins/plugin-s3/src/capabilities/blob-backend.ts
    - The host resolves the space's S3 Connection for writes and a credential per URI host for reads. github:dxos/dxos/packages/core/compute/compute-runtime/src/services/s3-host.ts#createS3Host
    - The backend PUTs to <spaceId>/<contentHash>, reusing the content hash as the payload hash. github:dxos/dxos/packages/core/echo/blob/src/s3/blob-backend.ts#createS3BlobBackend
    - getUrl presigns when a credential exists and returns the public URL otherwise. github:dxos/dxos/packages/core/echo/blob/src/s3/s3-client.ts#getObjectUrl
  note: |
    A signed read treats only 404 and 403 as a miss, as specified, but `isMiss` treats every 4xx on an unsigned read
    as a miss (R2 returns 400 for a private bucket), so get/has do not reject on other client errors there. The put
    path uses the first S3 Connection with a resolvable credential. No test exercises `createS3BlobBackend` or
    `createS3Host`; only the s3-client read primitives are tested.
```

```mdl
verdict SigV4: A hand-rolled WebCrypto SigV4 signer derives the region from the host and leaves content-length unsigned.
  status: done
  evidence: [github:dxos/dxos/packages/core/echo/blob/src/s3/sigv4.ts#signRequest, github:dxos/dxos/packages/core/echo/blob/src/s3/sigv4.ts#presignUrl, github:dxos/dxos/packages/core/echo/blob/src/s3/s3-uri.ts#regionFromHost, github:dxos/dxos/packages/core/echo/blob/src/s3/s3-client.ts#putObject]
